# Fork: minimal upstream surface

Goal: keep merges from [yuliskov/SmartTube](https://github.com/yuliskov/SmartTube) (and MediaServiceCore) small and predictable.

## Prefer isolation (in order)

1. **Fork-only files/modules** — e.g. `PlexServiceCore/`, `MediaSourceRegistry`, presenters under fork packages
2. **Thin hooks in upstream files** — one registry call, `isPlex()` guard, or dispatch; no large Plex/business logic inline
3. **Avoid** drive-by refactors, renames, or formatting of upstream code you did not need to touch

## MediaServiceCore

- No Plex code in MSC
- Do not extend `mediaserviceinterfaces` for Plex (adapters in the fork)
- Prefer `youtubeapi/` / upstream-compatible fixes; document in `MediaServiceCore/CHANGELOG_FORK.md`

## When editing an upstream file

Mark non-trivial fork blocks so conflicts are obvious:

```java
// FORK: Plex — skip YouTube-only UI (see fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md § Fork Touch Points)
if (video != null && video.isPlex()) {
    return;
}
// END FORK
```

- Use `// FORK: <short why>` … `// END FORK` for multi-line blocks
- Single-line hooks may use a trailing `// FORK: …`
- Do not wrap entire upstream methods; keep the marked region as small as possible

## After adding/changing a hook

1. Update **[Fork Touch Points](fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md#fork-touch-points)** and [`.cursor/skills/upstream-merge/reference.md`](../skills/upstream-merge/reference.md) if the file/area is new or the merge hint changed
2. Add a `[Unreleased]` entry per [changelog-fork](changelog-fork.mdc)

## Decision check (before coding)

- Can this live in a fork-only class with a 1–5 line call site? → do that
- Unsure whether to patch upstream? → propose the smaller-diff option first; wait for confirmation on larger upstream edits
